<template class="task-template">
    <section id="file-drop-section" class="section js-section u-category-system">
        <header class="section-header">
            <div class="section-wrapper">
                <h1>
                    <svg class="section-icon"><use xlink:href="assets/img/icons.svg#icon-system"></use></svg>
                    File Drop
                </h1>
                <h3>Drag &amp; drop files onto the window and resolve their <em>filesystem paths</em>.</h3>

                <p>
                    Electron removed the <code>File.path</code> augmentation in Electron 32; the path must be resolved
                    with <code>webUtils.getPathForFile</code>, which is only callable from a preload context. Electron.NET
                    ships a default preload that exposes it to your page as <code>window.electronNET.getPathForFile(file)</code> -
                    no setup needed.
                </p>

                <p>You find the sample source code in <code>Controllers\FileDropController.cs</code>.</p>
            </div>
        </header>

        <div class="demo">
            <div class="demo-wrapper">
                <button id="file-drop-demo-toggle" class="js-container-target demo-toggle-button">
                    Drop files onto the window
                    <div class="demo-meta u-avoid-clicks">Supports: Win, macOS, Linux <span class="demo-meta-divider">|</span> Process: Both</div>
                </button>
                <div class="demo-box">
                    <div id="file-drop-zone" class="demo-controls"
                         style="min-height:180px;display:block;padding:20px;text-align:center;border:2px dashed currentColor;">
                        <strong style="line-height:180px;">Drop some files here</strong>
                    </div>

                    <table style="width:100%;margin-top:20px;border-collapse:collapse;">
                        <thead>
                            <tr style="text-align:left;">
                                <th style="padding:8px;">Name</th>
                                <th style="padding:8px;">Size</th>
                                <th style="padding:8px;">Path (resolved with <code>getPathForFile</code>)</th>
                                <th style="padding:8px;"></th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody id="file-drop-list"></tbody>
                    </table>

                    <p>In this example the page resolves the filesystem path of each dropped file with <code>window.electronNET.getPathForFile(file)</code> and lets you reveal it in the file manager.</p>

                    <h5>Main Process (C#)</h5>
                    <pre><code class="csharp">Electron.IpcMain.On("open-dropped-folder", (path) =>
{
    Electron.Shell.ShowItemInFolderAsync(path.ToString());
});</code></pre>

                    <div class="demo-protip">
                        <h2>ProTip</h2>
                        <strong>Renderer.js Support</strong>
                        <p>With the default window options the page can also resolve paths directly, without any preload:</p>
                        <pre><code class="language-js">const { webUtils } = require('electron');

document.getElementById('drop-zone').addEventListener('drop', (event) =&gt; {
  event.preventDefault();
  const files = Array.from(event.dataTransfer.files).map((file) =&gt; ({
    name: file.name,
    path: webUtils.getPathForFile(file),
  }));
  console.log(files);
});</code></pre>
                        <p>
                            In hardened windows (<code>nodeIntegration: false</code> with context isolation or sandbox),
                            <code>require</code> is unavailable - use the <code>window.electronNET</code> bridge exposed
                            by the framework default preload instead, or provide your own preload via
                            <code>WebPreferences.Preload</code>.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <script>
            (function () {
                const { ipcRenderer } = require("electron");

                const dropZone = document.getElementById("file-drop-zone");
                const list = document.getElementById("file-drop-list");

                dropZone.addEventListener("dragover", (event) => {
                    event.preventDefault();
                    event.dataTransfer.dropEffect = "copy";
                    dropZone.style.background = "rgba(128,128,128,0.15)";
                });

                dropZone.addEventListener("dragleave", () => {
                    dropZone.style.background = null;
                });

                dropZone.addEventListener("drop", (event) => {
                    event.preventDefault();
                    dropZone.style.background = null;

                    list.innerHTML = "";

                    Array.from(event.dataTransfer.files).forEach((file) => {
                        const path = window.electronNET?.getPathForFile(file) ?? "";

                        const row = document.createElement("tr");

                        const nameCell = document.createElement("td");
                        nameCell.style.padding = "8px";
                        nameCell.innerText = file.name;
                        row.appendChild(nameCell);

                        const sizeCell = document.createElement("td");
                        sizeCell.style.padding = "8px";
                        sizeCell.innerText = file.size.toLocaleString();
                        row.appendChild(sizeCell);

                        const pathCell = document.createElement("td");
                        pathCell.style.padding = "8px";
                        pathCell.innerText = path || "(no path)";
                        row.appendChild(pathCell);

                        const actionCell = document.createElement("td");
                        actionCell.style.padding = "8px";
                        if (path) {
                            const button = document.createElement("button");
                            button.className = "demo-button";
                            button.innerText = "Show in folder";
                            button.addEventListener("click", () => {
                                ipcRenderer.send("open-dropped-folder", path);
                            });
                            actionCell.appendChild(button);
                        }
                        row.appendChild(actionCell);

                        list.appendChild(row);
                    });
                });
            }());
        </script>
    </section>
</template>
